      sound: "Granz produced the way he promoted: he put great soloists together and let them play. The JATP records kept the roar of the hall, honking tenor battles included, and his studio pairings—Getz with Peterson’s trio, Coleman Hawkins with Ben Webster—followed the same logic [5]. Fitzgerald’s Song Books were the opposite: carefully arranged studio productions with orchestras directed by arrangers such as Buddy Bregman and Nelson Riddle [5].",
