        "Argo also recorded the Jazztet of Art Farmer and Benny Golson and the trio of the pianist Ramsey Lewis. In 1965 the label was renamed Cadet to avoid confusion with a British label called Argo [1]. That year Lewis’s The In Crowd, recorded at the Bohemian Caverns in Washington, crossed over to the pop charts, and Cadet’s commercial peak, from 1965 to 1969, rode on Lewis, the arrangements of Richard Evans and Charles Stepney, and experiments such as Dorothy Ashby’s Afro-Harping and Marshall Chess’s psychedelic Cadet Concept [1].",
